1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,095
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:05,204
Did Walker destroy Haven?

3
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:08,438
EDUARDO: <i>This part of
the op is need-to-know.</i>

4
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:16,341
I come bearing gifts.

5
00:00:21,555 --> 00:00:23,456
Reunification with the mainland

6
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:25,252
<i>hangs on by a thread.</i>

7
00:00:25,392 --> 00:00:29,056
<i>Toxic chemicals rain down
onto the city, and the government</i>

8
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:30,528
cuts us adrift for good.

9
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:32,609
THOMPKINS: <i>The filtration system</i>

10
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:34,534
<i>that Lucius designed is working.</i>

11
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,279
LUCIUS: <i>It's not glamorous work,</i>

12
00:00:36,303 --> 00:00:39,137
but we are helping to save
the lives of thousands of people.

13
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:40,683
SELINA: <i>You're leaving Gotham.</i>

14
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,067
OSWALD: <i>I believe
the time has come</i>

15
00:00:42,175 --> 00:00:44,110
<i>for a change of scenery.</i>

16
00:00:44,545 --> 00:00:46,104
You found a way out of Gotham?

17
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:47,413
It's a submarine.

18
00:00:47,681 --> 00:00:52,676
OSWALD: <i>Jim Gordon and
Lee Thompkins are man and wife.</i>

19
00:00:53,186 --> 00:00:56,179
<i>He will never see
you as anything but</i>

20
00:00:56,323 --> 00:00:58,383
a dangerous woman
keeping his child

21
00:00:58,525 --> 00:00:59,525
<i>from him.</i>

22
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,689
Eduardo.

23
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,189
Walker.

24
00:01:03,764 --> 00:01:07,132
Professor Strange'll have
you fixed up in no time.

25
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:15,070
(whirring)

26
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:30,624
(labored breathing)

27
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:46,234
WALKER: <i>Rest easy, Eduardo.</i>

28
00:01:49,676 --> 00:01:52,145
I made you a promise
when I found you

29
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:53,679
in that hole in Peña Dura.

30
00:01:54,748 --> 00:01:57,149
<i>And I intend to keep it.</i>

31
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:01,245
To give you a true purpose

32
00:02:02,189 --> 00:02:04,886
and the strength
to see it through.

33
00:02:05,392 --> 00:02:09,488
However, I'm afraid this process

34
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:13,758
will be agonizing
and, unfortunately,

35
00:02:14,601 --> 00:02:16,229
quite lengthy.

36
00:02:18,205 --> 00:02:20,538
Apologies in advance.

37
00:02:24,778 --> 00:02:27,338
(squeaking)

38
00:02:54,441 --> 00:02:55,670
(labored breathing)

39
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:02,347
You're going to be reborn.

40
00:03:03,717 --> 00:03:06,551
And then you'll be
the bane of the unjust.

41
00:03:07,921 --> 00:03:09,412
The bane of the corrupt.

42
00:03:10,624 --> 00:03:13,651
The bane of anyone
who opposes us.

43
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,497
(screaming)

44
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:32,774
Radio confirmation.

45
00:03:32,979 --> 00:03:34,971
<i>General Wade's
landing craft docked.</i>

46
00:03:35,282 --> 00:03:37,217
His convoy's on
the way here now.

47
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:39,285
Reunification day is today.

48
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:42,417
Harv, that is great
news, but then what?

49
00:03:42,856 --> 00:03:44,415
Just 'cause we
rebuild some bridges

50
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,652
doesn't mean things are
gonna suddenly improve.

51
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,992
So, uh, future got you spooked?

52
00:03:50,297 --> 00:03:51,856
(sighs) Yeah, I guess.

53
00:03:52,432 --> 00:03:53,876
I mean, I want to believe
things are gonna get better,

54
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,100
but sometimes it's just hard
for me to see it, you know.

55
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:57,936
Can't say I understand.

56
00:03:58,271 --> 00:04:00,331
I don't have kids, at
least none that I know of.

57
00:04:01,007 --> 00:04:02,566
<i>But you got one coming,</i>

58
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:05,470
so we got no
choice but to believe.

59
00:04:06,379 --> 00:04:08,660
It's got to be better than what
we've been through, right?

60
00:04:09,483 --> 00:04:11,247
It damn well better be.

61
00:04:12,986 --> 00:04:16,616
Seven days in a row of
.07 water toxicity levels.

62
00:04:16,757 --> 00:04:18,020
Lucius' filters did the job.

63
00:04:18,358 --> 00:04:19,758
Eh, good work.
Hope it's not wasted.

64
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,620
Is there a reason to
think there's a problem?

65
00:04:21,695 --> 00:04:22,958
Jim's got a lot on his mind.

66
00:04:23,296 --> 00:04:24,696
What with Gotham
rejoining the world

67
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:26,529
and a baby coming
into the world next week.

68
00:04:26,666 --> 00:04:27,690
Give it a rest, Harvey.

69
00:04:27,834 --> 00:04:29,359
All joking aside.

70
00:04:30,036 --> 00:04:33,632
We're here because
of you. Mm-hmm.

71
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:36,300
And you're gonna be a
father. That's a future I'll take.

72
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:44,943
Over the past year,

73
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:47,777
you've all done good work.

74
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:52,389
We've made Gotham a safe
place for kids and families.

75
00:04:52,826 --> 00:04:55,421
We've given people the food
and medicine they needed.

76
00:04:56,997 --> 00:04:58,590
But it's not over yet.

77
00:04:59,833 --> 00:05:02,826
So, no matter what
General Wade says today,

78
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:05,895
the work continues.

79
00:05:07,841 --> 00:05:09,935
Give yourselves one
more round of applause.

80
00:05:12,946 --> 00:05:14,642
And get back to work.

81
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:24,716
Here they come.

82
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:49,014
Captain Gordon.

83
00:05:49,449 --> 00:05:51,077
Nice to finally meet
you in the flesh.

84
00:05:51,551 --> 00:05:53,543
General, welcome to Gotham.

85
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,712
Good that you've
reestablished some semblance

86
00:05:55,889 --> 00:05:57,448
of law and order around here.

87
00:05:57,791 --> 00:05:59,020
Seems like the Green Zone

88
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:01,453
stretches to every
corner of the island.

89
00:06:01,928 --> 00:06:04,762
General, Wayne Labs
show toxicity levels

90
00:06:04,898 --> 00:06:06,858
way below the threshold
the government set for us.

91
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:08,501
All due respect, Mr. Wayne,

92
00:06:08,902 --> 00:06:10,942
but I got to go with what
my people tell me on this.

93
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:13,767
♪♪♪♪

94
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:39,397
Cutting it a little
close, aren't we?

95
00:06:39,733 --> 00:06:40,894
Is that under 27 pounds,

96
00:06:41,034 --> 00:06:41,831
<i>13 ounces?</i>

97
00:06:41,935 --> 00:06:43,995
It can't possibly make
that big a difference.

98
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:47,083
It's only the difference
between getting off this island

99
00:06:47,107 --> 00:06:48,769
or sinking to the
bottom of the river.

100
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:51,674
Well, then Pengy can off-load
a few of his knickknacks.

101
00:06:51,811 --> 00:06:53,040
Not a chance.

102
00:06:53,647 --> 00:06:56,412
Because you know what's
worth its weight in gold?

103
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,618
- Gold.
- Ah!

104
00:07:00,186 --> 00:07:01,711
(groaning)

105
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:06,616
Congratulations!

106
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,760
(chuckles)

107
00:07:08,495 --> 00:07:11,158
Go to the clinic.
Go have your baby.

108
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:12,975
What? So the two
of you can hightail it

109
00:07:12,999 --> 00:07:15,025
off this rock without
me? I don't think so.

110
00:07:15,168 --> 00:07:18,195
I assure you we will
not launch without you.

111
00:07:18,538 --> 00:07:20,098
Ed and I will finish
making preparations

112
00:07:20,173 --> 00:07:22,768
and we will be ready to launch
the moment you get back here

113
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:24,878
with that little bundle of joy.

114
00:07:26,746 --> 00:07:28,544
Or unless I should
drive you to the clinic

115
00:07:28,715 --> 00:07:30,115
in light of your
delicate condition?

116
00:07:30,216 --> 00:07:32,776
I can do it. I'm
not that delicate.

117
00:07:33,186 --> 00:07:35,655
Remember that if you even think

118
00:07:35,922 --> 00:07:37,481
about double-crossing me.

119
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:45,107
It's very kind of you
to offer to drive her.

120
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,997
I knew she would
never accept my help.

121
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:51,276
Should I start the engine?

122
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:52,791
One less passenger
to worry about.

123
00:07:52,906 --> 00:07:54,135
Oh, two, actually.

124
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,132
You are so right.

125
00:07:56,609 --> 00:07:57,941
(chuckles)

126
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:21,926
(gasps, chuckles)

127
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:24,169
Found it.

128
00:08:24,637 --> 00:08:25,969
Ah, well done, Miss Kyle.

129
00:08:27,907 --> 00:08:29,068
All right, let's have a look.

130
00:08:31,077 --> 00:08:32,807
Uh, here we are.

131
00:08:34,714 --> 00:08:37,980
Oh, so this guy's the architect
who designed Wayne Manor?

132
00:08:38,118 --> 00:08:39,279
Yes, right.

133
00:08:39,853 --> 00:08:43,119
With the reunification, a new
Wayne Manor must follow.

134
00:08:44,557 --> 00:08:47,618
And it'll be just
like the old one?

135
00:08:48,061 --> 00:08:50,292
Oh, nothing is just like it was.

136
00:08:51,765 --> 00:08:54,792
So why are we
looking at the old plans?

137
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:58,262
Perhaps I'm not ready
to let go of the past.

138
00:09:02,175 --> 00:09:03,541
Well, if it makes
you feel better,

139
00:09:03,676 --> 00:09:06,043
I wish I could blow up my past.

140
00:09:08,815 --> 00:09:10,181
Well, maybe you will.

141
00:09:11,618 --> 00:09:12,995
One day, when you
build something new,

142
00:09:13,019 --> 00:09:15,545
the past will
always be part of it.

143
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:17,815
As for me,

144
00:09:17,991 --> 00:09:19,789
now Master Bruce is grown,

145
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:24,190
building a new manor might
be my last great service to him.

146
00:09:25,999 --> 00:09:26,999
A home.

147
00:09:28,835 --> 00:09:30,064
And then what?

148
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:33,234
You retire?

149
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:36,041
No.

150
00:09:39,279 --> 00:09:42,909
I will stand guard,
as I've always done.

151
00:09:48,321 --> 00:09:49,949
I thought this was all settled.

152
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,090
This is bull.

153
00:09:51,224 --> 00:09:52,783
My results are accurate, Jim.

154
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:55,171
BULLOCK: <i>We don't know this
general. Maybe he's with Walker.</i>

155
00:09:55,195 --> 00:09:58,324
Let's not get carried away.
Bruce, go and check on the tech.

156
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,126
(radio crackles)

157
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,360
(sighs)

158
00:10:03,036 --> 00:10:04,129
This is Gordon.

159
00:10:04,871 --> 00:10:05,930
THOMPKINS: <i>It's Lee.</i>

160
00:10:06,639 --> 00:10:07,639
Everything okay?

161
00:10:09,709 --> 00:10:10,836
Barbara just showed up here,

162
00:10:11,244 --> 00:10:12,244
<i>in labor.</i>

163
00:10:12,712 --> 00:10:13,805
You're kidding.

164
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:15,945
THOMPKINS: <i>You
better come quick.</i>

165
00:10:20,653 --> 00:10:21,814
Are you okay?

166
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:25,386
Yeah. Yeah.

167
00:10:28,094 --> 00:10:29,926
<i>I'll try to get over
there as soon as I can.</i>

168
00:10:31,231 --> 00:10:32,231
<i>Try to.</i>

169
00:10:32,265 --> 00:10:35,394
Um... try to wait for me.

170
00:10:36,269 --> 00:10:38,295
It doesn't really work that way.

171
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:39,905
I know.

172
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,307
Okay.

173
00:10:43,109 --> 00:10:44,133
<i>Wait.</i>

174
00:10:46,246 --> 00:10:47,246
I love you.

175
00:10:48,681 --> 00:10:50,115
(labored breathing)

176
00:10:51,384 --> 00:10:52,784
I love you, too.

177
00:10:53,419 --> 00:10:54,419
Jim!

178
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:56,822
<i>What? What's wrong?</i>

179
00:10:57,223 --> 00:10:58,223
We did it.

180
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:00,085
You did it. We
got through it, Jim.

181
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,160
WADE: <i>Captain.</i>

182
00:11:02,362 --> 00:11:03,362
All clear.

183
00:11:03,429 --> 00:11:04,658
Congratulations.

184
00:11:05,198 --> 00:11:06,826
Reunification can begin.

185
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:11,133
Well, I'm glad I can
make you so happy.

186
00:11:12,405 --> 00:11:13,873
Funny thing is, sir,

187
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:16,340
that's just the second
best news I've gotten today.

188
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,338
(distant rumble)

189
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:20,279
What's that?

190
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:21,680
(bang)

191
00:11:23,149 --> 00:11:24,447
- Jim.
- Incoming.

192
00:11:27,086 --> 00:11:28,679
Everybody get back!

193
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:31,154
Get inside! Get inside!

194
00:11:36,796 --> 00:11:37,796
Go, go.

195
00:11:49,976 --> 00:11:51,945
(gunfire)

196
00:12:03,489 --> 00:12:05,321
(grunting)

197
00:12:08,228 --> 00:12:09,924
(bones crunch)

198
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:11,063
(man screaming)

199
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:13,756
Eduardo?

200
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:17,264
Not anymore.

201
00:12:49,802 --> 00:12:51,532
All right, people, listen up.

202
00:12:52,305 --> 00:12:55,070
I want squads headed
for Knights Stadium,

203
00:12:55,308 --> 00:12:57,470
Yeavley Park, and
Granton Station.

204
00:12:57,877 --> 00:13:00,210
Work your way out. We
got to find him, people.

205
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:03,346
Bloody hell happened?

206
00:13:03,483 --> 00:13:04,849
Seems that Jim's old army buddy

207
00:13:04,984 --> 00:13:06,475
wasn't quite as
dead as we'd hoped.

208
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:08,848
I got squads covering
the north side.

209
00:13:08,988 --> 00:13:10,165
<i>They're sweeping from Coventry</i>

210
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:12,134
down to Miller Harbor,
but they could be anywhere.

211
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:13,235
Well, give us an area to search

212
00:13:13,259 --> 00:13:14,579
- and we'll get
it covered.
- Uh...

213
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:16,058
<i>Take Reatton,</i>

214
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:17,475
work your way to
South City Park.

215
00:13:17,563 --> 00:13:20,032
Looks like you're not done
protecting Bruce yet, Alfred.

216
00:13:25,271 --> 00:13:27,206
(rasping)

217
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:33,245
Eduardo.

218
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:36,582
What did Walker do to you?

219
00:13:39,185 --> 00:13:42,087
When I was in Peña
Dura prison, Jim,

220
00:13:42,355 --> 00:13:44,153
<i>the guards played a game.</i>

221
00:13:45,525 --> 00:13:47,187
They'd choose one of us...

222
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:48,852
and they buried us alive.

223
00:13:49,562 --> 00:13:51,997
They'd take bets on whether
you could dig your way out.

224
00:13:52,131 --> 00:13:55,033
But then they'd bury you deeper.

225
00:13:56,102 --> 00:13:57,570
And play again.

226
00:13:59,405 --> 00:14:00,964
I was the champion.

227
00:14:02,909 --> 00:14:03,968
To survive that...

228
00:14:04,977 --> 00:14:06,969
I had to stop being human.

229
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:12,212
I had to become...
something else.

230
00:14:14,287 --> 00:14:15,380
I became Bane.

231
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:18,987
<i>Only I didn't know it yet.</i>

232
00:14:19,325 --> 00:14:22,887
But she knew and she
showed me the way.

233
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:26,124
If the world is
full of monsters,

234
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:28,257
the only way to defeat them...

235
00:14:28,601 --> 00:14:30,536
is to become one yourself.

236
00:14:32,638 --> 00:14:34,038
I'm sorry.

237
00:14:35,007 --> 00:14:36,475
You were a good soldier.

238
00:14:37,643 --> 00:14:38,643
Hmm.

239
00:14:38,911 --> 00:14:40,209
Don't pity me, Jim.

240
00:14:41,647 --> 00:14:43,513
We are building the future.

241
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,353
She's given me a
purity of mission.

242
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:47,349
And unlike the army,

243
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:50,013
she is willing to
carry things out.

244
00:14:51,958 --> 00:14:53,984
A new world is coming.

245
00:14:54,494 --> 00:14:55,985
Strong...

246
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,425
merciless...

247
00:14:59,132 --> 00:15:00,259
unyielding.

248
00:15:00,533 --> 00:15:02,263
I've heard it all before.

249
00:15:03,536 --> 00:15:04,536
Not gonna happen.

250
00:15:07,106 --> 00:15:09,541
And how are you
going to stop me, Jim?

251
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:11,076
<i>Not me.</i>

252
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:14,040
You kidnapped Bruce Wayne
and a general of the U.S. Army.

253
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:17,376
You talk about your future,
Eduardo, but you don't have one.

254
00:15:18,518 --> 00:15:20,111
But Eduardo's dead, Jim.

255
00:15:22,288 --> 00:15:23,916
There is only Bane now.

256
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:26,017
(door opens)

257
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:29,060
Rise.

258
00:15:31,631 --> 00:15:33,429
I said rise!

259
00:15:34,534 --> 00:15:35,934
WALKER: <i>Not so formal.</i>

260
00:15:36,469 --> 00:15:38,097
Captain and I are acquainted.

261
00:15:40,506 --> 00:15:42,099
Get the other one.

262
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:48,274
I recognize your voice,

263
00:15:48,414 --> 00:15:49,734
but I don't know
what to call you.

264
00:15:51,083 --> 00:15:52,517
<i>I know it's not Walker.</i>

265
00:15:53,686 --> 00:15:55,177
So who are you?

266
00:15:56,522 --> 00:15:58,650
That's a good question.

267
00:15:59,425 --> 00:16:03,590
Perhaps Bruce Wayne can
help us figure that one out.

268
00:16:03,729 --> 00:16:05,561
(footsteps approach)

269
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,635
You okay?

270
00:16:10,736 --> 00:16:12,227
(panting): Yeah.

271
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:16,469
You want hostages?

272
00:16:17,276 --> 00:16:19,108
You've got me and a
general of the U.S. Army.

273
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:20,371
Let him go.

274
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:22,114
<i>This has nothing to do with him.</i>

275
00:16:23,249 --> 00:16:25,218
"This has nothing
to do with him"?

276
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:28,379
But, Captain, you don't
even know what "this" is.

277
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:33,050
This, everything
I have done here,

278
00:16:33,192 --> 00:16:35,320
is about punishing Gotham.

279
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:39,163
For the sins of Bruce Wayne.

280
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:42,591
You can start now.

281
00:16:46,472 --> 00:16:47,997
No... no!

282
00:16:49,408 --> 00:16:52,071
(grunts, groans)

283
00:16:52,211 --> 00:16:53,543
And again.

284
00:16:54,547 --> 00:16:55,547
(grunts)

285
00:16:57,550 --> 00:16:58,550
So...

286
00:16:59,619 --> 00:17:01,178
Bruce Wayne.

287
00:17:02,321 --> 00:17:04,290
I'm thinking of a name.

288
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,788
Can you guess whose it is?

289
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,560
What?

290
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:11,224
Wrong. And again.

291
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:12,388
(shouts)

292
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:15,267
Want to take another guess?

293
00:17:20,806 --> 00:17:23,708
Farewell, my beloved Gotham.

294
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:26,536
City of my birth.

295
00:17:27,747 --> 00:17:30,808
Parting is such sweet sorrow.

296
00:17:33,452 --> 00:17:35,387
Though I leave you today...

297
00:17:36,255 --> 00:17:38,486
my heart will always remain.

298
00:17:39,158 --> 00:17:41,718
I do so hate goodbyes.

299
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:42,619
Well, you're in luck.

300
00:17:42,762 --> 00:17:44,373
- We're not going anywhere.
- What are you
talking about?

301
00:17:44,397 --> 00:17:46,696
Engine won't start; pressure
regulator valve's missing.

302
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,066
Or rather it's stolen.

303
00:17:51,671 --> 00:17:55,267
Barbara!

304
00:17:55,775 --> 00:17:57,801
(exhaling heavily)

305
00:17:58,144 --> 00:17:59,373
Blood pressure's normal.

306
00:18:00,546 --> 00:18:02,481
I'm glad something
about this is normal.

307
00:18:03,316 --> 00:18:05,547
So how long's this gonna
take, Doc, soup to nuts?

308
00:18:06,385 --> 00:18:07,717
Are you in a hurry or something?

309
00:18:08,721 --> 00:18:10,280
No, it's just that, uh...

310
00:18:11,457 --> 00:18:12,823
I just feel like you've been...

311
00:18:13,159 --> 00:18:14,627
so great about this, and,

312
00:18:15,127 --> 00:18:16,572
you know, it's been
awkward as hell for you,

313
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:19,657
and... I haven't even
really said thank you.

314
00:18:20,466 --> 00:18:22,226
I don't expect a thank
you from you, Barbara.

315
00:18:22,301 --> 00:18:23,779
Then perhaps the best
thank you would be for me

316
00:18:23,803 --> 00:18:25,601
to get out of here
as soon as possible.

317
00:18:29,375 --> 00:18:30,707
Whatever's on your mind...

318
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:33,176
the health of the
baby comes first.

319
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,641
I know that.

320
00:18:35,881 --> 00:18:37,873
So, long haul or
short, we're here.

321
00:18:38,217 --> 00:18:40,209
Until you have a healthy
baby in your arms.

322
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,515
That's all I want.

323
00:18:44,457 --> 00:18:45,550
(softly): Okay.

324
00:18:53,766 --> 00:18:55,132
(exhales sharply)

325
00:18:55,735 --> 00:18:57,169
- (grunts)
- Stop it!

326
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,599
A name, a person.

327
00:19:01,173 --> 00:19:03,335
The reason this
is all happening.

328
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:06,412
Can't you guess yet?

329
00:19:06,612 --> 00:19:08,547
I don't know!

330
00:19:13,586 --> 00:19:15,885
If you want to
punish me, then do it.

331
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:17,517
Hurt me, not him.

332
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:19,786
I am hurting you.

333
00:19:19,925 --> 00:19:22,724
- (panting)
- There's nothing
more painful

334
00:19:22,928 --> 00:19:25,329
than seeing your friends suffer.

335
00:19:26,532 --> 00:19:28,194
But he's more
than just a friend,

336
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:29,802
isn't he, Bruce?

337
00:19:30,369 --> 00:19:33,498
Jim Gordon's been
like a father to you.

338
00:19:34,306 --> 00:19:35,306
Oh.

339
00:19:35,441 --> 00:19:39,378
How awful it must be to
watch another father die.

340
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:41,276
(strained exhale)

341
00:19:42,882 --> 00:19:45,215
Who am I doing this for?

342
00:19:45,351 --> 00:19:46,751
Say the name.

343
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:49,715
(grunts)

344
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,190
(groans)

345
00:19:54,293 --> 00:19:56,455
When the ones you love die...

346
00:19:57,530 --> 00:20:00,466
it's like a part of
yourself is cut off...

347
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:02,233
forever.

348
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,428
(sobs)

349
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:05,868
You know that.

350
00:20:08,774 --> 00:20:10,868
So why do I hate you so much?

351
00:20:11,310 --> 00:20:13,211
Who was cut away from me?

352
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,408
Last chance.

353
00:20:15,548 --> 00:20:17,608
(whimpers)

354
00:20:32,998 --> 00:20:34,227
Yes.

355
00:20:35,634 --> 00:20:36,932
Now you know.

356
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:41,268
Say his name.

357
00:20:41,974 --> 00:20:43,306
Say it.

358
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:45,903
Ra's al Ghul.

359
00:20:48,013 --> 00:20:50,380
This is revenge for his death.

360
00:20:53,519 --> 00:20:54,953
And who am I?

361
00:20:56,989 --> 00:20:58,582
You're his daughter.

362
00:21:03,662 --> 00:21:05,893
My name is Nyssa al Ghul.

363
00:21:06,899 --> 00:21:10,529
And revenge is just the
beginning of what I want.

364
00:21:19,378 --> 00:21:20,903
(Bane rasping)

365
00:21:22,548 --> 00:21:24,779
NYSSA: <i>The League of
Shadows is everywhere.</i>

366
00:21:25,417 --> 00:21:28,285
<i>Did you think my father's
mission would die with him?</i>

367
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:32,488
Humankind will be
purged of weakness.

368
00:21:33,526 --> 00:21:36,291
I'm just starting
with you and yours.

369
00:21:38,898 --> 00:21:40,059
You're right.

370
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,666
I killed Ra's.

371
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:46,505
So whatever you need to do...

372
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:47,834
do it to me.

373
00:21:52,077 --> 00:21:53,077
No.

374
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:56,415
<i>You can't take all the
blame for killing my father.</i>

375
00:21:56,715 --> 00:22:00,846
I mean, you did
have some help, right?

376
00:22:02,521 --> 00:22:06,356
<i>Someone who quite literally
gave you a helping hand.</i>

377
00:22:08,794 --> 00:22:10,592
- What are you doing?
- (yells)

378
00:22:17,403 --> 00:22:19,031
Well done, Barbara.

379
00:22:25,411 --> 00:22:26,845
Go get Barbara Kean.

380
00:22:29,548 --> 00:22:30,548
Eduardo...

381
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:35,344
She's pregnant.

382
00:22:36,789 --> 00:22:38,417
She's carrying a child.

383
00:22:39,458 --> 00:22:40,790
A child.

384
00:22:43,562 --> 00:22:46,930
One soul's future
weighed against the world's.

385
00:22:48,801 --> 00:22:50,736
Your concern seems petty, Jim.

386
00:22:55,507 --> 00:22:57,806
If he touches a hair
on that child's head,

387
00:22:58,444 --> 00:22:59,844
I will destroy
everything you have.

388
00:22:59,979 --> 00:23:03,916
I don't have anything left,
just my father's mission.

389
00:23:09,588 --> 00:23:12,558
Bane wants you to
join that mission with us.

390
00:23:14,526 --> 00:23:16,927
To see the world as he sees it.

391
00:23:17,763 --> 00:23:20,528
- Never.
- STRANGE:
Never say never,

392
00:23:20,666 --> 00:23:22,100
<i>- Captain Gordon.</i>
- No!

393
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,903
NYSSA: <i>How does it feel, Bruce,</i>

394
00:23:29,541 --> 00:23:31,840
knowing that all
of this is your fault?

395
00:23:33,846 --> 00:23:36,873
Tell me. I'd
really like to know.

396
00:23:38,817 --> 00:23:40,945
(screams)

397
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:44,420
(groaning)

398
00:23:44,690 --> 00:23:46,420
There must be something
you can give me.

399
00:23:46,558 --> 00:23:48,424
We're out of the
drugs that you need.

400
00:23:49,128 --> 00:23:50,858
It's okay. You're almost there.

401
00:23:51,196 --> 00:23:53,396
I'll get you some ice chips
so you don't get dehydrated.

402
00:23:53,532 --> 00:23:54,966
Gee, thanks.

403
00:23:59,071 --> 00:24:00,071
Lee.

404
00:24:01,006 --> 00:24:02,065
Ed.

405
00:24:03,175 --> 00:24:04,973
Don't worry, I'm
not here for you.

406
00:24:06,745 --> 00:24:09,909
But for the record,
you stabbed me first.

407
00:24:10,716 --> 00:24:12,184
If you two are quite done,

408
00:24:12,518 --> 00:24:14,714
we are actually
here for Barbara.

409
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:18,186
Or more precisely,
what she stole from us.

410
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:20,702
I don't know what this
is about, and I don't care.

411
00:24:20,726 --> 00:24:22,170
You two need to get
out of here right now.

412
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:23,719
(chuckles) Gladly.

413
00:24:23,862 --> 00:24:25,057
<i>Just as soon as Barbara</i>

414
00:24:25,197 --> 00:24:27,928
gives us the...
What's it called?

415
00:24:28,067 --> 00:24:29,660
- Pressure regulator valve.
- Right.

416
00:24:30,035 --> 00:24:31,035
That.

417
00:24:31,603 --> 00:24:32,603
(sighs)

418
00:24:33,038 --> 00:24:35,507
I should have known that
you would try to screw us over.

419
00:24:35,641 --> 00:24:39,009
You only noticed because
you tried to screw me over first.

420
00:24:39,478 --> 00:24:40,969
Second, technically.

421
00:24:41,113 --> 00:24:43,105
Okay, she's in the
middle of having a baby.

422
00:24:43,549 --> 00:24:45,017
And we are in
the middle of trying

423
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:47,676
to leave Gotham,
and we can't do that

424
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:49,880
without a crucial
part of the submarine

425
00:24:50,222 --> 00:24:52,191
which will ferry us
all away from here!

426
00:24:52,524 --> 00:24:53,635
That's why you
were in such a rush

427
00:24:53,659 --> 00:24:55,992
- to get out of here.
- As are we.

428
00:24:58,864 --> 00:25:02,028
Hand over the part... now.

429
00:25:02,267 --> 00:25:04,065
Don't point that at the baby.

430
00:25:04,570 --> 00:25:06,732
What? No, I did not!

431
00:25:06,872 --> 00:25:10,536
I... I was merely trying
to make a general

432
00:25:10,676 --> 00:25:12,036
threatening gesture
with a firearm.

433
00:25:12,077 --> 00:25:13,722
But you did, though. You
pointed the gun at the baby.

434
00:25:13,746 --> 00:25:17,683
All right, fine. I'm sorry!
Now give us what we want!

435
00:25:17,816 --> 00:25:20,615
No! You think I'm stupid
enough to have the part on me?

436
00:25:20,786 --> 00:25:22,755
It's hidden away,
somewhere safe.

437
00:25:22,888 --> 00:25:25,949
And if you think you can
torture me into telling you where,

438
00:25:26,125 --> 00:25:28,651
there is literally
nothing more painful

439
00:25:28,794 --> 00:25:32,162
than what I am going
through right now!

440
00:25:32,297 --> 00:25:33,060
(explosion)

441
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,962
(screaming in distance)

442
00:25:36,568 --> 00:25:38,059
NURSE: <i>Hey, you
stay out of here.</i>

443
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,203
This is a hospital.

444
00:25:39,638 --> 00:25:40,662
(neck snaps)

445
00:25:42,174 --> 00:25:43,233
(bell dings)

446
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:47,642
Barbara Kean,

447
00:25:48,313 --> 00:25:50,544
<i>your time is up.</i>

448
00:25:51,183 --> 00:25:52,981
<i>There's no place
for you to hide.</i>

449
00:25:54,019 --> 00:25:55,180
No one will save you.

450
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,948
No mercy that will spare you.

451
00:25:58,123 --> 00:26:01,184
You simply cannot
run from your sins.

452
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,826
And you cannot run from me.

453
00:26:15,841 --> 00:26:17,241
What do you want from me?

454
00:26:18,110 --> 00:26:19,237
(chuckles)

455
00:26:22,081 --> 00:26:25,677
Let me let you in on
a little military secret.

456
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:30,614
It's called Special Order 386.

457
00:26:31,757 --> 00:26:34,955
In the event that Gotham
is irretrievably lost,

458
00:26:35,627 --> 00:26:37,858
a contingency plan
was put in place

459
00:26:38,130 --> 00:26:40,998
to reduce the city to rubble.

460
00:26:44,837 --> 00:26:45,361
No.

461
00:26:45,704 --> 00:26:47,172
There are still
innocent people here.

462
00:26:47,306 --> 00:26:50,174
You asked me
what I want from you.

463
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:55,714
I want you to
suffer, Bruce Wayne.

464
00:26:56,849 --> 00:26:58,977
And then I want you to die.

465
00:27:02,020 --> 00:27:05,047
Spend a little time
with that thought.

466
00:27:06,959 --> 00:27:08,359
We'll be starting soon.

467
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:15,929
♪♪♪♪

468
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:18,632
- Who are those guys?
- No idea.

469
00:27:19,004 --> 00:27:21,030
Exactly how many people
have you screwed over?

470
00:27:21,173 --> 00:27:22,971
Present company excluded.

471
00:27:23,275 --> 00:27:25,210
There are 79 people
in this building.

472
00:27:25,344 --> 00:27:27,664
Well, fortunately, they seem
to only be trying to kill one.

473
00:27:27,946 --> 00:27:30,006
So, by all means, let's
gather 'round the target.

474
00:27:30,149 --> 00:27:31,173
- All right.
- (groaning)

475
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:33,046
Maybe we can cut
through the abandoned wing

476
00:27:33,185 --> 00:27:34,949
and we can get to the
ambulance bay that way.

477
00:27:35,087 --> 00:27:36,131
Might take some time, but...

478
00:27:36,155 --> 00:27:37,795
Oh, if only there were
two able-bodied men

479
00:27:37,856 --> 00:27:38,856
who could buy us some.

480
00:27:38,957 --> 00:27:41,222
And why, pray tell, should
we risk our necks for you?

481
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,360
(straining): Chivalry?

482
00:27:42,427 --> 00:27:43,895
(laughs)

483
00:27:44,096 --> 00:27:46,031
But if that's too much,
remember, if I die,

484
00:27:46,165 --> 00:27:47,997
you will never
find that sub part.

485
00:27:48,133 --> 00:27:49,133
Fine.

486
00:27:49,835 --> 00:27:51,098
We'll keep them busy.

487
00:27:51,703 --> 00:27:52,823
We'll meet you at the docks.

488
00:27:52,938 --> 00:27:54,031
Thank you.

489
00:27:59,144 --> 00:28:00,840
- What?
- Keep them busy?

490
00:28:01,013 --> 00:28:03,380
I only brought enough
ammunition for a light firefight,

491
00:28:03,749 --> 00:28:06,116
not to repel a
paramilitary assault.

492
00:28:06,251 --> 00:28:08,311
What should we use, bedpans?

493
00:28:09,154 --> 00:28:10,231
I was actually
thinking of something

494
00:28:10,255 --> 00:28:12,986
a little more... flammable.

495
00:28:13,992 --> 00:28:15,290
♪♪♪♪

496
00:28:15,994 --> 00:28:17,724
(both laugh)

497
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,234
(grunts)

498
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:51,855
Why, Captain Gordon,
how nice that you're awake.

499
00:28:52,831 --> 00:28:55,062
You picked the
losing side, Strange.

500
00:28:56,268 --> 00:28:59,329
The army's coming
to Gotham. Help me,

501
00:28:59,471 --> 00:29:01,269
and you can do what you do best:

502
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:02,967
survive.

503
00:29:04,176 --> 00:29:05,735
I happen to think more

504
00:29:05,877 --> 00:29:08,210
of Ms. al Ghul's
chances for success

505
00:29:08,347 --> 00:29:09,906
than a man in your...

506
00:29:10,215 --> 00:29:11,215
well...

507
00:29:11,984 --> 00:29:13,145
position.

508
00:29:14,319 --> 00:29:16,515
You really think she can
take on the entire army?

509
00:29:16,888 --> 00:29:18,447
As a matter of fact, I do.

510
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:21,317
With my help.

511
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:25,492
You are just a few
modifications away

512
00:29:25,831 --> 00:29:28,391
from being a mighty
soldier in her forces.

513
00:29:28,834 --> 00:29:31,827
Not unlike your
friend, Eduardo...

514
00:29:32,404 --> 00:29:36,068
I will help you to
realize your full potential,

515
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:39,277
give you true strength.

516
00:29:40,312 --> 00:29:41,075
I'll pass.

517
00:29:41,213 --> 00:29:43,148
<i>Consent is hardly</i>

518
00:29:43,282 --> 00:29:44,910
a prerequisite.

519
00:29:45,417 --> 00:29:48,148
We will begin...

520
00:29:49,288 --> 00:29:51,223
with, uh, physical improvements.

521
00:29:51,356 --> 00:29:52,483
(groans softly)

522
00:29:55,294 --> 00:29:56,294
Sorry.

523
00:29:56,828 --> 00:29:58,922
And finish...

524
00:30:00,198 --> 00:30:03,930
with certain mental adjustments.

525
00:30:07,339 --> 00:30:08,398
(elevator bell dings)

526
00:30:09,007 --> 00:30:10,498
(rasping)

527
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,553
(cheers)

528
00:30:28,994 --> 00:30:31,088
(Bane rasping)

529
00:30:50,315 --> 00:30:51,926
Your contractions are
about a minute apart.

530
00:30:51,950 --> 00:30:53,230
We've got to get
you out of here.

531
00:30:53,452 --> 00:30:54,452
(screams)

532
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:55,282
(grunts)

533
00:30:55,420 --> 00:30:57,889
(pained yelling)

534
00:30:58,457 --> 00:30:59,857
Nice shot!

535
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:02,627
(yelling)

536
00:31:05,097 --> 00:31:06,097
Keep breathing.

537
00:31:06,131 --> 00:31:07,155
(panting)

538
00:31:36,995 --> 00:31:37,995
(grunts quietly)

539
00:31:55,213 --> 00:31:57,182
♪♪♪♪

540
00:32:05,323 --> 00:32:06,382
(panting softly)

541
00:32:06,525 --> 00:32:08,050
Some try to hide,
some try to cheat.

542
00:32:08,193 --> 00:32:09,913
- (sighs)
- But time will
let us always meet.

543
00:32:10,028 --> 00:32:11,155
What am I?

544
00:32:11,630 --> 00:32:13,326
- Pregnant lady with a gun?
- Death.

545
00:32:13,465 --> 00:32:14,524
But close enough.

546
00:32:15,634 --> 00:32:17,603
So, where to now?

547
00:32:18,136 --> 00:32:19,434
Well, I believe...

548
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:21,968
we have a sub to catch.

549
00:32:22,207 --> 00:32:25,041
- (chuckles)
- How long have you had that?

550
00:32:25,177 --> 00:32:26,988
Long enough to know she'd
never let it out of her sight.

551
00:32:27,012 --> 00:32:29,311
(laughs)

552
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:34,251
And you stuck around long enough

553
00:32:34,553 --> 00:32:37,717
to risk both of our
lives to save Barbara's?

554
00:32:40,358 --> 00:32:41,519
Or was it to protect Lee?

555
00:32:42,327 --> 00:32:44,887
Do you want me to answer that or
do you want sail away from here?

556
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,657
Bon voyage.

557
00:32:53,405 --> 00:32:56,307
Oh, those bastards have
stolen the damn sub part!

558
00:32:56,441 --> 00:32:57,465
You mean, stole it back.

559
00:32:57,609 --> 00:32:59,441
Whose side are you on?

560
00:32:59,578 --> 00:33:01,376
Clearly, I'm on the
baby's side, Barbara.

561
00:33:01,513 --> 00:33:04,210
- Ooh!
- What was your plan, anyway?

562
00:33:05,116 --> 00:33:07,585
You were going to be a fugitive
with Nygma and Penguin?

563
00:33:07,719 --> 00:33:10,587
Well, I'm not exactly the stay-
at-home-and-bake-apple-pie type.

564
00:33:10,755 --> 00:33:14,055
Yeah, running off on a submarine
seemed like a great alternative.

565
00:33:18,463 --> 00:33:22,730
Barbara, you can live here.
You can have this baby here.

566
00:33:23,235 --> 00:33:25,329
Jim is not taking the
baby away from you.

567
00:33:27,305 --> 00:33:28,671
You really believe that?

568
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:32,204
You really think
Captain Jim Gordon

569
00:33:32,344 --> 00:33:34,711
is gonna let a
criminal raise his kid?

570
00:33:39,751 --> 00:33:41,549
People are already
shooting at my baby.

571
00:33:42,454 --> 00:33:43,717
I have to protect him...

572
00:33:44,756 --> 00:33:45,756
or her.

573
00:33:46,424 --> 00:33:47,790
I have to be strong.

574
00:33:49,094 --> 00:33:52,223
Right, being strong does not
mean you have to be a criminal.

575
00:33:54,399 --> 00:33:55,399
Jim will help you.

576
00:33:57,335 --> 00:33:58,701
And so will I if you'll let me.

577
00:33:59,604 --> 00:34:00,731
Well, that's just weird.

578
00:34:01,473 --> 00:34:02,473
I know.

579
00:34:03,275 --> 00:34:05,506
Hey, baby, this
is your Auntie Lee.

580
00:34:05,777 --> 00:34:07,439
Mommy tried to kill
her once, maybe twice.

581
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:08,774
- (both laugh)
- All right.

582
00:34:09,114 --> 00:34:10,124
Okay, that's enough of that.

583
00:34:10,148 --> 00:34:11,582
Come on. We got to keep moving.

584
00:34:13,485 --> 00:34:14,817
I think this is happening now.

585
00:34:16,588 --> 00:34:19,353
(screams)

586
00:34:19,491 --> 00:34:21,255
(panting)

587
00:34:25,463 --> 00:34:27,364
(panting)

588
00:34:35,407 --> 00:34:36,773
(whimpers softly)

589
00:34:40,612 --> 00:34:41,612
(screams)

590
00:34:41,646 --> 00:34:43,080
SOLDIER: <i>What's
going on in there?</i>

591
00:34:44,849 --> 00:34:45,849
(yells)

592
00:34:54,492 --> 00:34:56,358
This is Bruce Wayne.
Can anyone read me?

593
00:34:59,598 --> 00:35:00,598
(grunts)

594
00:35:01,399 --> 00:35:03,868
This is Bruce Wayne. Does
anyone at the GCPD read me?

595
00:35:05,503 --> 00:35:07,472
<i>This is Bruce Wayne.
Can anyone read me?</i>

596
00:35:08,473 --> 00:35:10,874
Bruce, it's Alfred. Where
the devil are you? Over.

597
00:35:11,576 --> 00:35:13,772
Some abandoned
mansion in North Side Park.

598
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,112
- On my way.
<i>- No.</i>

599
00:35:15,246 --> 00:35:16,305
I'll get out myself.

600
00:35:16,481 --> 00:35:17,761
I need you to get to the clinic.

601
00:35:17,816 --> 00:35:18,613
The clinic?

602
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:20,514
<i>It's Ra's al Ghul's
daughter, Alfred.</i>

603
00:35:21,219 --> 00:35:23,745
<i>She wants revenge. She
mutated Eduardo Dorrance</i>

604
00:35:23,888 --> 00:35:25,254
<i>and sent him after Barbara.</i>

605
00:35:25,390 --> 00:35:26,483
Oh, gosh.

606
00:35:27,192 --> 00:35:28,285
I'm fine.

607
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,892
I need you to get to
Barbara and the baby.

608
00:35:33,665 --> 00:35:36,829
Now, you're going to
feel a slight discomfort.

609
00:35:37,235 --> 00:35:40,467
That's the stimulant I've given
you to prepare your muscles.

610
00:35:40,672 --> 00:35:43,506
<i>You'll need it for what
comes next, which,</i>

611
00:35:44,776 --> 00:35:47,610
I'm afraid, is going
to be excruciating.

612
00:35:50,248 --> 00:35:52,581
(machine whirring)

613
00:35:52,717 --> 00:35:56,176
(grunts)

614
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:00,655
Do you feel that?

615
00:36:02,193 --> 00:36:03,252
Yes.

616
00:36:07,599 --> 00:36:10,296
(Gordon groans)

617
00:36:11,569 --> 00:36:12,569
(grunts)

618
00:36:21,546 --> 00:36:23,913
There's that fighting spirit

619
00:36:24,249 --> 00:36:26,514
I've always admired so much.

620
00:36:26,651 --> 00:36:27,778
<i>Now, if you'll excuse me,</i>

621
00:36:28,253 --> 00:36:29,846
there's an alarm I must sound.

622
00:36:30,255 --> 00:36:31,255
(grunts)

623
00:36:33,458 --> 00:36:34,824
(panting)

624
00:36:37,529 --> 00:36:38,656
(grunts)

625
00:36:40,965 --> 00:36:43,085
- What the hell are you doing?
- Checking to make sure

626
00:36:43,268 --> 00:36:45,430
Strange doesn't have one
of those chips in your head.

627
00:36:46,404 --> 00:36:47,463
We need to hurry up,

628
00:36:47,605 --> 00:36:49,245
get out of here before
he trips the alarm.

629
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:51,605
(alarm blaring)

630
00:36:51,743 --> 00:36:52,743
Come on.

631
00:36:58,516 --> 00:36:59,727
Alfred and GCPD are on their way

632
00:36:59,751 --> 00:37:01,031
<i>- to the clinic.</i>
- Where's Nyssa?

633
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:02,386
<i>I don't know.</i>

634
00:37:02,921 --> 00:37:05,281
But she's planning on using
the military to wipe out Gotham.

635
00:37:05,523 --> 00:37:07,253
I can order them to stand down.

636
00:37:07,992 --> 00:37:09,358
Then let's get you out of here.

637
00:37:17,502 --> 00:37:18,697
THOMPKINS: She's beautiful.

638
00:37:18,970 --> 00:37:20,438
Congratulations.

639
00:37:21,539 --> 00:37:22,539
Hi, there.

640
00:37:23,475 --> 00:37:25,467
Guess I'm-a have figure
out what to call you.

641
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:27,943
- (chuckles softly)
- (sniffles)

642
00:37:28,646 --> 00:37:29,646
Thank you.

643
00:37:43,661 --> 00:37:45,789
(baby crying)

644
00:37:50,802 --> 00:37:52,828
- (Thompkins gasps)
- (tires screech)

645
00:37:55,006 --> 00:37:57,305
- Come on.
- Get in the car now.

646
00:37:57,742 --> 00:37:58,742
I'll hold him off.

647
00:37:58,977 --> 00:38:00,309
SELINA: <i>Alfred and I got this.</i>

648
00:38:01,513 --> 00:38:02,753
ALFRED: <i>Selina, get in the car.</i>

649
00:38:02,981 --> 00:38:04,813
<i>- Selina, get back in the car!</i>
- No.

650
00:38:05,450 --> 00:38:06,450
Go.

651
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:08,547
Oh, my, look at you.

652
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:10,367
You're a big'un, ain't you?

653
00:38:10,989 --> 00:38:12,719
Bloody baby bully,
let's see what you got.

654
00:38:12,857 --> 00:38:14,689
(grunting)

655
00:38:26,571 --> 00:38:27,971
(grunting)

656
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:34,472
Dirty bastard.

657
00:38:35,346 --> 00:38:37,315
(Alfred screams)

658
00:38:46,858 --> 00:38:49,919
(grunting)

659
00:38:52,564 --> 00:38:53,564
No!

660
00:38:55,033 --> 00:38:56,033
Alfred.

661
00:38:58,002 --> 00:38:59,402
Alfred.

662
00:39:02,540 --> 00:39:04,668
(whispers): Alfred. No.

663
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,910
Somebody help!

664
00:39:07,445 --> 00:39:08,879
(panting)

665
00:39:08,980 --> 00:39:11,074
Somebody. Oh, no.

666
00:39:30,401 --> 00:39:31,801
SOLDIER: A-ten-hut!

667
00:39:38,576 --> 00:39:39,703
<i>Welcome back, General.</i>

668
00:39:40,411 --> 00:39:42,778
Get me a secure line
to the mainland now.

669
00:39:44,449 --> 00:39:46,077
Jim! Hey.

670
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,478
Just got word from Lee.

671
00:39:49,153 --> 00:39:51,418
She and Barbara made
it out of the clinic okay.

672
00:39:52,423 --> 00:39:53,789
And your baby daughter, too.

673
00:39:56,527 --> 00:39:58,996
- Congratulations.
- They're going to The Sirens.

674
00:40:00,698 --> 00:40:03,497
- You just had a baby girl,
brother. Say something.
- (laughs)

675
00:40:10,642 --> 00:40:12,042
Just can't believe it.

676
00:40:12,777 --> 00:40:14,439
We won, didn't we? It's over.

677
00:40:14,612 --> 00:40:17,514
We did, and she's gonna have
a better world because of it.

678
00:40:17,682 --> 00:40:19,844
She is. I promise.

679
00:40:20,652 --> 00:40:21,449
Is Alfred with them?

680
00:40:21,586 --> 00:40:22,586
Didn't say.

681
00:40:23,521 --> 00:40:25,046
This is General Wade.

682
00:40:26,557 --> 00:40:29,994
I am authorizing
Special Order 386.

683
00:40:30,695 --> 00:40:31,458
No!

684
00:40:31,596 --> 00:40:33,792
Gotham City is lost.

685
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:35,764
Begin your bombing
run on my order.

686
00:40:35,900 --> 00:40:37,900
- Wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait.
- Arrest them.

687
00:40:39,604 --> 00:40:40,867
You can't do this.

688
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,105
Take them away.

689
00:40:42,740 --> 00:40:44,003
You can't do this!

690
00:40:47,979 --> 00:40:49,219
THOMPKINS: Okay, nice and slow.

691
00:40:51,149 --> 00:40:53,084
(baby fussing)

692
00:40:55,520 --> 00:40:56,613
(gasps)

693
00:41:05,697 --> 00:41:07,723
- Barbara Kean.
- Run!

694
00:41:12,704 --> 00:41:14,866
It's nice to finally meet you.

695
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:18,566
My name is Nyssa al Ghul.

696
00:41:21,045 --> 00:41:23,514
I believe you knew my father.

697
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:31,598
I don't understand how the
general could have been chipped.

698
00:41:31,622 --> 00:41:33,702
I didn't see a scar on the
back of his neck. Did you?

699
00:41:33,825 --> 00:41:35,259
No. Strange must've hidden it.

700
00:41:35,593 --> 00:41:38,119
Nyssa let us escape. She
knew we'd bring the general here

701
00:41:38,262 --> 00:41:39,753
and do her dirty work for her.

702
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:46,503
BULLOCK: What now, Jim?

703
00:41:46,537 --> 00:41:49,598
Son, if you're gonna
stick a gun in my face,

704
00:41:49,807 --> 00:41:52,641
you should at least know
you're doing it wrong.

705
00:41:55,947 --> 00:41:57,279
Come on, let's go.

706
00:41:57,615 --> 00:41:59,550
(helicopter blades whirring)

707
00:42:08,559 --> 00:42:12,826
(explosions)
